data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"# Reply to dispatch d002\\n\\n## What I did\\n\\nImplemented the greeting feature exactly as specified:\\n\\n1. **`src/greet.py`** — added `greet(name)` which returns `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`.\\n   - `greet(\\\"World\\\")` → `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`\\n2. **`tests/test_greet.py`** — unittest-based tests covering:\\n   - A normal name: `greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`\\n   - The empty string: `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n   - The test file prepends `../src` to `sys.path` so it imports `greet.py`;\\n     no `__init__.py` was needed for discovery.\\n\\nNothing outside `src/greet.py` and `tests/test_greet.py` was touched.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nCommand run from `~/subject`:\\n\\n    python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n\\nResult (exit code 0):\\n\\n    ..\\n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    Ran 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\n    OK\\n\\n## Commit\\n\\n- Branch: `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`\\n- Commit: `968fc1f` — \\\"Add greet() and unit tests (dispatch d002)\\\"\\n- Working tree clean; branch differs from base `1fdce0c` by this one commit.\\n\\nNo blockers; nothing left undone.\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-reply.md\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_11","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789936193,"id":"chatcmpl-17eb9f2ba68f4ff3aa13d7158300d8c7","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

